  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Castanospermine and the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, mediated through multiple intermediate targets. Castanospermine is directly linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and by Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate. Both of these intermediates are also targets of the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This indicates that Castanospermine may influence the proteasome through a series of biochemical pathways, potentially affecting its function or stability. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a strong, though not absolute, correlation between Castanospermine and the proteasome subunit, likely due to the shared biological role in protein degradation and regulation. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear, necessitating further experimental validation."
